From: xuning <1729984965@qq.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/rockchip: dw-hdmi: drive enable GPIO high at probe

Vendor driver requests enable-gpios with GPIOD_ASIS and only switches it
to output when the encoder is enabled. On HD-RK3588-CORE the external
HDMI buffer/level-shifter needs enable asserted earlier so HPD and DDC
can work before the first modeset. Request as GPIOD_OUT_HIGH at probe.

Signed-off-by: xuning <1729984965@qq.com>
---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/dw_hdmi-rockchip.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/dw_hdmi-rockchip.c
@@ -2046,8 +2046,9 @@
 		return PTR_ERR(hdmi->link_clk);
 	}
 
+	/* Assert early so HPD/DDC through external buffer work before modeset */
 	hdmi->enable_gpio = devm_gpiod_get_optional(hdmi->dev, "enable",
-						    GPIOD_ASIS);
+						    GPIOD_OUT_HIGH);
 	if (IS_ERR(hdmi->enable_gpio)) {
 		ret = PTR_ERR(hdmi->enable_gpio);
 		dev_err(hdmi->dev, "failed to request enable GPIO: %d\n", ret);
